---

🔗 Key Relationships

👤 User → Customer

1:1 (or 1:N depending on system design)


🌍 Customer → Greenhouse

1:N


🌡️ Greenhouse → Sensor Source

1:N


📡 Sensor Source → Sensor

1:N over time (but only 1 active at a time)


🌱 Sensor Source → Plant

1:N


👉 This is the critical design decision

> Plants are tied to Sensor Source, not Sensor




---

🔥 Important Rules Enforced by This ERD

1. Sensor Replacement

New sensor can reuse same sensor_source_id

Old sensor becomes inactive



---

2. Only One Active Sensor Per Source

UNIQUE (sensor_source_id) WHERE status = 'active'


---

3. Plants Follow the Source

Switching sensors → plants stay the same

Different source → different plants



---

4. Data Integrity

All environmental readings tied to:

sensor_source_id



---

🧠 Why This ERD Works Well

✔ Supports sensor replacement
✔ Keeps historical consistency
✔ Separates hardware from logical data stream
✔ Allows multiple plants per environment
✔ Clean and scalable


